Partner led the \SJ against notrump and dummy plays low. You are third hand, holding the \ST — which card do you play?

When you have chosen, click NEXT. [choose-card ST] [NEXT]

[show NESW]

Unblock — play the \ST under the jack. Partner’s jack asks about the ten, and dropping it clears the way: partner’s \SQ-9-8 run once the ace and king are forced out, with no bare ten to block them. (Without the ten you would give count instead, marking it with declarer.)}

